WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.370
-Tonight was the second night
of the second round

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.770
of Democratic
presidential debates.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.873
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.710
♪♪

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.779
Of course, everyone's
watching these debates

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.181
to see who will emerge
as the leading contenders,

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.983
and that apparently includes
Donald Trump,

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.385
who said last night
during an interview on C-SPAN

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.153
that he'd be watching
the debates

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:22.621
and offered this hot take.

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:24.757
-I'll be watching
the debates tonight.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:28.795
You know, if I didn't,
you'd say, "I can't imagine."

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.196
You know, I would like to know

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.664
who I'm going to be
running against.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.532
Maybe you'll tell me
after this interview, right?

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:34.934
-You tell me.
-I don't know.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.270
I mean, I would think
the four or five top ones

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.838
would seem to have a big edge.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.474
You have some people that
shouldn't even be wasting time,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.776
but I would think
the four or five top ones

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.611
would be the ones
that would be, you know,

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:48.681
certainly have the best chance
of getting in.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.082
-Oh.

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.751
Is that your expert analysis?

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:56.956
That the top four or five
candidates have the best chance?

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.459
It's like a commentator at
halftime during the NBA Finals

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:02.795
going, "I think it's either
going to be the Raptors

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.431
or the Warriors, Ernie.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:10.569
Unless a third outside team
sneaks in there."

00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:13.506
Of course, the dynamic
at the first night's debate

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.808
ended up being mostly Elizabeth
Warren and Bernie Sanders

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.244
fending off a bunch of underdog
moderates taking shots at them

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.279
like former Congressman
and soon-to-be

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.482
former president candidate
John Delaney.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.284
By the end of the night,
he looked like the guy

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:29.221
who comes in third
on "Jeopardy!"

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:31.557
Even when Warren and Sanders
weren't talking,

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:34.494
they were winning.
Bernie's strategy, of course,

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.896
involved a lot of arm throwing
and finger wagging

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:41.267
like he was reaching to turn off
an imaginary light switch.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.570
And at one point,
when Elizabeth Warren's plan

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.105
for a wealth tax came up,
she literally smiled

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.941
and rubbed her hands together
in glee.

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.744
Look at how excited she is
to tear this guy apart.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.013
It's like in Looney Tunes
when you're starving

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.116
and you see a giant turkey leg.

00:01:57.116 --> 00:02:01.254
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.523
We spent the most part
of our day

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.759
figuring out
how that would look.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.395
Nonetheless, the underdogs
have been desperate to spin

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.063
their debate performances
last night.

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:13.766
For example, there was this
moment when Congressman Tim Ryan

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.435
thought he scored a point on
Bernie during a feisty exchange

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.337
on the climate crisis.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:21.640
-What do you do with an industry
that knowingly,

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.510
for billions of dollars
in short-term profits,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.080
is destroying this planet?

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.116
I say that is criminal activity.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.717
That cannot be allowed
to continue.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.419
-Thank you, Senator Sanders.
Congressman, your response.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.488
-Well, yeah, I would --
I would just say --

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.024
I didn't say we couldn't
get there will 2040, Bernie.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.359
You don't have to yell.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.294
-Uh, I'm sorry,.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.995
Have you met Bernie Sanders?

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:45.497
Of course, he has to yell.

00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:46.766
Yelling is his brand.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.835
He read bedtime stories
to his kids,

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.971
and they didn't sleep
until they were 35.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.807
But Ryan thought
that was such a killer line

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.943
that today he kind of turned it
into a campaign slogan of sorts

00:02:57.943 --> 00:03:00.445
by selling stickers
on his website that say

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:01.847
"You don't have to yell."

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.250
And while I understand
the gist of his point,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.720
I'm not sure about the timing.
I mean, if there was ever a time

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.922
to yell in American politics,
it's now.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.292
That would be like the captain
of the "Titanic"

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:16.296
putting up a "no swimming" sign
after hitting the iceberg.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.898
Both the moderates
and the moderators

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.767
tried to take shots
at Bernie and Warren
over Medicare for All.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.836
Pundits seemed obsessed
with getting them to say

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.506
that they would raise taxes,
even though the reality is

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.274
that healthcare costs
would be much lower,

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.177
which is how it works in a bunch
of major industrialized nations.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.147
And that led to this combative
post-debate interview last night

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:37.716
in which Warren deftly battled
with MSNBC's Chris Matthews.

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:41.087
-They won't have any more money.
When you're paying...

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.821
You guys dodged that tonight.

00:03:42.821 --> 00:03:44.624
-No, no, it's not a dodge.
It's about where --

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.392
-'Cause Jake Tapper kept saying,

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.361
"How much are your taxes
going to go up?"

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.262
And you'd say -- You'd say --

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.632
-How much are your costs
going to go down?

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:55.234
-No, no. Different question.
How much will your taxes go up?

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.970
-No, it's how much
of your costs.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.939
It's how much families
end up saving.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.074
-I know that argument.
-It's not just an argument.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.644
-But you're covering it.
But will you pay more in taxes?

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.746
Why don't you want to answer
that question?

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.747
-Because it's a question --
-Because Jake said tonight

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:10.316
that's a Republican
talking point.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.685
It's not a Republican talking
point. It's a question.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.354
-It's a question about where

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.088
people are going to come out
economically.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:18.290
The question is not
do you have health insurance

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.192
or not have health insurance.

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:23.061
The question is, how much
are you going to have to dig

00:04:23.061 --> 00:04:24.596
in your pocket to pay?

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:27.132
-I know that's the answer
that you like to give, but --

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.268
-No. It is the answer.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:32.405
-When Elizabeth Warren says,
"No, it is the answer,"

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.740
then that's the answer.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.775
She was a Harvard professor.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.743
You're trying to school her
on healthcare.

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:40.646
I didn't know
that the "MS" in "MSNBC"

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:43.082
stood for "mansplain."

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.286
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:51.157
She had to fend off Matthews

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:54.527
like Chris Pratt fending off
a velociraptor.

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:56.262
Then in another
post-debate interview,

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.864
CNN tried to get Warren to take
a shot at former Vice President

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.167
Joe Biden, who is currently
leading in the polls,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.969
but she firmly batted it down.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.870
-For people who are trying
to choose between you

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.739
and former Vice President Biden,
why are you a better candidate?

00:05:07.739 --> 00:05:11.076
-Well, I'm not here to dis
any other Democrat.

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.879
Just get somebody else
for that job. That's not me.

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:16.315
-Wow. You know you asked
a bad question when you found

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:19.385
the one job Elizabeth Warren
won't do.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.521
That was like when you ask the
waiter for bread, and he goes,

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.091
"This is not my section."

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.560
It's certainly the case
that, according to the polls,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.161
Biden was the front-runner
coming in,

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.797
and all eyes seemed to be on him
and Senator Kamala Harris.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:34.233
Everyone was asking, would
we see Harris destroy a man

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.868
live on national TV again?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.937
Would Biden try
to fend off questions

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.006
by flashing those big ol'
pearly whites again?

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.308
And would New York City mayor
Bill de Blasio be there

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:45.143
to yell over everyone
like a guy trying to hail a cab

00:05:45.143 --> 00:05:46.578
in a rainstorm?

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:49.048
"Hey! Hey! Over here!
Hey! I was here first!"

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:53.219
"Okay. Dang.
You don't have to yell."

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.387
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.122
And even before...

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:57.590
[ Applause ]

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.692
Even before tonight's
debate started,

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.594
things got a little weird
when the chair

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.729
of the Democratic National
Committee, Tom Perez,

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.731
tried to fire up the crowd

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:07.933
and call out Senate Majority
Leader Mitch McConnell

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:10.236
for blocking bills that
Democrats passed in the House,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:13.138
and he used a version
of a nursery rhyme.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:18.010
-Old McConnell had a farm.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.179
E-I-E-I-O.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:23.281
And on that farm,
he kept all those bills

00:06:23.281 --> 00:06:24.950
that passed the House.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.386
E-I-E-I-O.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.722
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.330
-I think I speak for everyone
when I say...

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.498
E-I-E-I-No.

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.438
That was the worst...

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:48.807
That was the worst
Weird Al cover ever!

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.510
You can't beat Mitch McConnell
with nursery rhymes.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:55.013
Nursery rhymes power him, like
the villain in a horror movie.

00:06:55.013 --> 00:06:57.349
Whenever he speaks
on the floor of the Senate,

00:06:57.349 --> 00:07:00.285
you can hear children creepily
singing in the background.

00:07:00.285 --> 00:07:05.057
-♪ Down came the rain
and washed the spider out ♪

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:06.358
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.358 --> 00:07:09.127
-Perez also spoke about the fact
that he once had a job

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:11.798
working on a garbage truck
to take a shot at Trump.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.666
-I worked on the back
of a trash truck,

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.400
so I know garbage when I see it!

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:19.672
And, folks, this administration
is a dumpster fire!

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.908
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:23.142
-It's true, but I would say

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.877
Trump is less like
a dumpster fire

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:27.746
and more like the guy who sets
the dumpster on fire

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:29.682
for the insurance money.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.952
Boom. Dumpster's gone.
Now we collect.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.220
And then once again,
just as they did last night,

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.656
CNN introduced all
the candidates individually,

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:39.658
and, once again,
the lesser-known candidates

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:41.327
polling in single digits
had to follow

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:44.063
the more popular candidates who
got much bigger crowd reactions.

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:46.966
-Former Vice President
Joe Biden.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:50.168
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.168 --> 00:07:52.238
Senator Kamala Harris.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:56.508
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:07:56.508 --> 00:07:59.445
Mayor Bill de Blasio.

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:01.514
[ Subdued applause ]

00:08:01.514 --> 00:08:04.583
-Man, it's tough for de Blasio
to have to follow those two.

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:06.051
It's like
if you were at Comic-Con

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.187
and they introduced
Iron Man, Captain America,

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:10.690
and then Ben Affleck's
Daredevil.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.325
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.427
And once they got out there with
all eyes on Harris and Biden,

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:18.797
Biden was caught on a mic
trying that ol' Joe Biden charm

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:21.433
to preempt the confrontation.

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:24.970
-Hey, Joe.
-Go easy on me, kid.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.472
-Hey, man,
if you don't want to seem old,

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:30.776
maybe don't talk like you're
in a Humphrey Bogart movie.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:35.280
"Go easy on me, kid.
We'll always have Detroit."

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.151
[ Laughs ]

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:43.122
Saved my Humphrey Bogart
impression for the live show.

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.591
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:48.094
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:50.096 --> 00:08:52.331
"Say, say!"

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:54.699
Next, you're going to
start telling people

00:08:54.699 --> 00:08:57.069
you're 76 years young.

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:59.371
Right off the bat,
CNN was desperately interested

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:01.373
both in framing
the issue of healthcare

00:09:01.373 --> 00:09:03.475
from a right-wing perspective
and also of getting

00:09:03.475 --> 00:09:06.178
Harris and Biden to go after
each other on that issue.

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:09.214
-This week, you released
a new healthcare plan

00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:11.417
which would preserve
private insurance

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:13.486
and take 10 years to phase in.

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:17.023
Vice President Biden's campaign
calls your plan

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:19.925
"A have it
every which way approach,"

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:22.894
and says it's just part
of a confusing pattern

00:09:22.894 --> 00:09:25.264
of equivocating about
your healthcare stance.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.665
What do you say to that?

00:09:26.665 --> 00:09:29.035
-Well, they're probably confused
because they've not read it.

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:31.370
-Vice President Biden,
your response.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.838
-Well, my response is that

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.074
the Senator's
had several plans so far.

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:40.179
You can't beat President Trump
with double talk on this plan.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.847
-Your response, Senator Harris?
-Absolutely.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.448
Unfortunately,
Vice President Biden,

00:09:43.448 --> 00:09:45.651
you're just simply inaccurate
in what you're describing.

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:49.121
-Senator Harris, thank you.
Vice President, your response.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:54.059
-The plan, no matter how you cut
it, costs $3 trillion.

00:09:54.059 --> 00:09:56.028
-CNN was so desperate
to get them to fight,

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.096
they were like Romans
at the Colosseum.

00:09:58.096 --> 00:10:00.399
"Healthcare plans,
he says yours is foolish.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:04.036
You say his is cruel.
Now fight for our pleasure."

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:13.479
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:16.014
It seemed like every question
was framed as an attack

00:10:16.014 --> 00:10:17.249
from someone else onstage.

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.117
In fact, at one point,
Cory Booker

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:21.721
pointed out the boxing-match
nature of the questions

00:10:21.721 --> 00:10:23.189
by bringing up Donald Trump.

00:10:23.189 --> 00:10:25.024
-Well, first of all, let me
just say that the person

00:10:25.024 --> 00:10:27.059
that's enjoying
this debate most right now

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:29.628
is Donald Trump as we pit
Democrats against each other

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:34.500
while he is working right now to
take away Americans' healthcare.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.736
-Trump might be enjoying
the fighting, but there's no way

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:39.004
he's enjoying all this
specific policy details.

00:10:39.004 --> 00:10:41.339
Trump watches policy debates
the way the rest of us

00:10:41.339 --> 00:10:42.508
watch foreign movies.

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:43.942
"I don't know
what they're talking about,

00:10:43.942 --> 00:10:46.011
but the fight scenes
are amazing."

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:47.746
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:10:47.746 --> 00:10:51.049
In fact, the CNN moderators...

00:10:51.049 --> 00:10:53.085
The moderators were so
interested in getting

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:55.321
the candidates to go after
each other that, all night,

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:57.089
they were cutting people off
before they could

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:58.990
finish their answers
just so they could go

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.759
to someone else for a response.

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:01.893
-...coverage like
mental healthcare --

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:03.328
-Thank you, Mr. Mayor.

00:11:03.328 --> 00:11:04.729
-...to make it harder for you
to afford it --

00:11:04.729 --> 00:11:06.298
-Thank you, Senator Gillibrand.

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:08.900
-...demoralizing us in the face
of the real enemy here --

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.369
-Thank you, Senator.

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:12.304
-Our plan covers everyone...
-Thank you, Senator.

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:14.239
-...and gives people choice.
-Thank you, Senator.

00:11:14.239 --> 00:11:16.275
-My God, this debate was like
a game of "Taboo"

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:19.044
where every word
was forbidden.

00:11:19.044 --> 00:11:20.979
"I believe we need health --"
[ Buzzer ]

00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:22.881
"I'm sorry, Senator,
you can't say the word health.

00:11:22.881 --> 00:11:24.950
It's on the card."
[ Laughter ]

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.452
In fact, there were multiple
times when Biden

00:11:26.452 --> 00:11:28.053
was answering a question
and then literally

00:11:28.053 --> 00:11:29.688
just stopped talking in
the middle of a sentence

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:30.922
when he was cut off.

00:11:30.922 --> 00:11:32.458
-The Biden Plan,
which is Obamacare --

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:34.426
-Thank you, Mr. Vice President.
Thank you.

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:37.429
-It's a crime,
and it's not one that in fact --

00:11:37.429 --> 00:11:39.131
-Thank you, Mr. Vice President.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:39.131 --> 00:11:41.934
-Beyond the cost of inflation
from this point on.

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.235
And the --
-Thank you, Mr. Vice President.

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:44.970
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.239
-He gave up so easily.
Didn't even finish his --

00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:49.308
It's like when your grandpa
tries to speak up

00:11:49.308 --> 00:11:51.977
at the dinner table
and no one hears him.

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:55.214
"I have a story about
restauran-- Oh, never mind."

00:11:55.214 --> 00:11:56.615
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:57.949
How you gonna fight for America

00:11:57.949 --> 00:11:59.318
when you can't even
fight through the timer?

00:11:59.318 --> 00:12:01.219
Also, you know if you end up
as the nominee

00:12:01.219 --> 00:12:02.488
and you're running
against Donald Trump,

00:12:02.488 --> 00:12:04.222
he's never gonna stop talking.

00:12:04.222 --> 00:12:06.592
You're gonna
have to talk over him.

00:12:06.592 --> 00:12:07.693
Have you seen him?

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:09.161
His mouth never stops moving.

00:12:09.161 --> 00:12:10.562
He's always
fighting with reporters

00:12:10.562 --> 00:12:11.964
and doing that thing

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:13.832
where he draws little boxes
with his hands.

00:12:13.832 --> 00:12:15.201
[ Laughter ]

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:17.736
"I was watching the debate
tonight on a TV

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:20.439
shaped like this,
but then I got bored

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.741
and switched
to 'The Bachelorette.'"

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:24.509
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.509 --> 00:12:26.211
One of the big divides

00:12:26.211 --> 00:12:28.347
in the debate
was over health insurance,

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:30.215
with the more progressive
candidates on stage

00:12:30.215 --> 00:12:32.451
wanting to expand Medicare
through various versions

00:12:32.451 --> 00:12:34.886
of Medicare for All,
but Biden's plan is more modest,

00:12:34.886 --> 00:12:36.922
claiming he would allow people
to keep their private insurance

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:38.290
if they like it.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:42.294
-The idea that this is somehow
a bad idea,

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.729
no one has to keep
their private insurance.

00:12:44.729 --> 00:12:46.131
But if they like
their insurance,

00:12:46.131 --> 00:12:47.766
they should be able to keep it.

00:12:47.766 --> 00:12:51.236
Nothing is demanded in my plan
that there be private insurance.

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:54.406
It says if the 160 million
people who have it

00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:56.308
say they like
their employer insurance,

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:58.444
they should have
a right to have it.

00:12:58.444 --> 00:13:00.746
-I'm sorry, but who likes
their private insurance?

00:13:00.746 --> 00:13:03.181
Nobody likes going to the E.R.
for a sprained ankle

00:13:03.181 --> 00:13:05.718
and then getting 58 envelopes
in the mail from Anthem.

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:07.219
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:08.687
I keep hearing this
talking point from moderates.

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:11.290
I've never heard anyone say,
"You can take my HMO

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.958
when you pry it from my cold,
dead hands,

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:14.292
which will be probably
be pretty soon

00:13:14.292 --> 00:13:15.794
because it doesn't
cover my meds."

00:13:15.794 --> 00:13:17.195
[ Laughter ]

00:13:17.195 --> 00:13:19.031
Later, Biden took on de Blasio
over the price

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:21.033
of Medicare for All,
claiming it would cost too much,

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:22.534
even though several candidates
have laid out

00:13:22.534 --> 00:13:25.003
specific, detailed plans
for how they would pay for it.

00:13:25.003 --> 00:13:27.206
And Biden used this line
on de Blasio.

00:13:27.206 --> 00:13:30.542
-The fact of the matter is
that there will be a deductible.

00:13:30.542 --> 00:13:32.344
It will be a deductible
on your paycheck.

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:35.514
Bernie acknowledges.
Bernie acknowledges.

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:41.019
$30 trillion
has to ultimately be paid,

00:13:41.019 --> 00:13:43.455
and I don't know what math
you do in New York,

00:13:43.455 --> 00:13:46.058
I don't know what math
you do in California,

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:48.327
but I tell you,
that's a lot of money.

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:51.930
-Be careful, because the most
common math equation in New York

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.166
is adding "Go" to "F yourself."

00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:57.802
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:13:57.802 --> 00:14:01.240
Biden...

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.475
Biden also pushed back
on criticisms

00:14:03.475 --> 00:14:04.676
of his more moderate plan

00:14:04.676 --> 00:14:07.312
and busted out
one of his old catch phrases.

00:14:07.312 --> 00:14:08.747
-What we've got
is a public option

00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:11.083
that, in fact, would allow
anybody to buy in.

00:14:11.083 --> 00:14:12.952
No one has to keep
their private insurance.

00:14:12.952 --> 00:14:14.653
They can buy into this plan.

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:18.256
And they can buy into it
with a $1,000 deductible

00:14:18.256 --> 00:14:21.660
and never pay more than 8.5%
of their income when they do it.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.263
And if they don't have any
money, they'll get in free.

00:14:24.263 --> 00:14:26.832
So this idea
is a bunch of malarkey.

00:14:26.832 --> 00:14:28.900
-There it is!
Mwah!

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:32.270
"A bunch of malarkey"
is Joe Biden's "More cowbell."

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:33.705
[ Cheers ]
And I love it.

00:14:33.705 --> 00:14:36.274
But again, it does make him
seem a little old.

00:14:36.274 --> 00:14:38.343
It's something
you expect to hear shouted

00:14:38.343 --> 00:14:40.212
from atop an old-timey bicycle.

00:14:40.212 --> 00:14:43.048
"5 cents for a nickelodeon?
That's a bunch of malarkey!"

00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:44.549
[ Laughter ]

00:14:44.549 --> 00:14:46.552
The debate then shifted
to criminal justice reform

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:50.022
with a specific focus on Biden's
record on several bills,

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:52.090
including the 1994 crime bill.

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:53.959
First,
Biden seemed to get confused

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.460
and gave Booker a new title.

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:58.230
-The fact is that the bills
that the president --

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.799
that -- excuse me --
the future president here --

00:15:00.799 --> 00:15:02.901
that the Senator's
talking about...

00:15:02.901 --> 00:15:04.436
-Wait. What?
Go back.

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:05.570
[ Laughter ]

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.672
Did he just endorse Cory Booker?
[ Laughter ]

00:15:07.672 --> 00:15:09.942
Did he forget that he's also
running for president?

00:15:09.942 --> 00:15:11.276
[ Laughter ]

00:15:11.276 --> 00:15:13.278
"Oh, what?
This is a presidential debate?

00:15:13.278 --> 00:15:15.414
Oh, I'm just here to mix it up
and have fun.

00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:18.249
It's malarkey time!"
[ Laughter ]

00:15:18.249 --> 00:15:21.753
"Let's get malarkey."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:21.753 --> 00:15:25.691
Then, Biden actually tried
to question booker's record

00:15:25.691 --> 00:15:28.560
as mayor of Newark, and it
did not end well for Biden.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:31.664
-We have a system right now
that's broken,

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:33.198
and if you want
to compare records,

00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:35.633
and, frankly,
I'm shocked that you do,

00:15:35.633 --> 00:15:37.535
I am happy to do that.

00:15:37.535 --> 00:15:39.037
-Why did you announce
in the first day

00:15:39.037 --> 00:15:43.008
a zero-tolerance policy
of stop-and-frisk

00:15:43.008 --> 00:15:46.611
and hire Rudy Giuliani's guy
in 2007

00:15:46.611 --> 00:15:48.680
when I was trying to get rid
of the crack cocaine --

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.582
-Well, Mr. Vice President,
there's a saying

00:15:50.582 --> 00:15:52.383
in my community --
you're dipping into the Kool-Aid

00:15:52.383 --> 00:15:53.985
and you don't even
know the flavor.

00:15:53.985 --> 00:15:57.790
-Damn. There is no way Biden
even knows what that means.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.024
[ Laughter ]

00:15:59.024 --> 00:16:02.827
Because I am 35 years
younger than him

00:16:02.827 --> 00:16:04.496
and I don't know
what that means.

00:16:04.496 --> 00:16:05.631
[ Laughter ]

00:16:05.631 --> 00:16:07.165
Biden probably
took it literally.

00:16:07.165 --> 00:16:09.435
"Kool-Aid?
I can't have all that sugar!"

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:10.802
[ Laughter ]

00:16:10.802 --> 00:16:13.404
Then, finally, the debate moved
on to the climate crisis.

00:16:13.404 --> 00:16:15.640
Several candidates have signed
on to the Green New Deal.

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:18.277
The moderators asked
Senator Kirsten Gillibrand

00:16:18.277 --> 00:16:20.011
if such an ambitious plan
was possible,

00:16:20.011 --> 00:16:21.547
and she busted out
this one-liner.

00:16:21.547 --> 00:16:23.615
-You are co-sponsor
of the Green New Deal,

00:16:23.615 --> 00:16:28.153
which includes the guarantee
of a job with medical leave,

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:30.822
paid vacations,
and retirement security

00:16:30.822 --> 00:16:32.524
for everyone in America.

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:34.426
Explain how that's realistic.

00:16:34.426 --> 00:16:36.628
-So, the first thing
that I'm gonna do

00:16:36.628 --> 00:16:40.265
when I'm president is I'm gonna
Clorox the Oval Office.

00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:42.301
-Okay, first of all,
I don't think it's legal

00:16:42.301 --> 00:16:44.603
to use bleach
on an active crime scene.

00:16:44.603 --> 00:16:45.671
[ Laughter ]

00:16:45.671 --> 00:16:49.141
Secondly...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:49.141 --> 00:16:53.078
...you're definitely gonna need
something stronger than Clorox.

00:16:53.078 --> 00:16:56.215
I would try burning sage
or holding a seance.

00:16:56.215 --> 00:16:58.383
And you're gonna need
a belt sander

00:16:58.383 --> 00:17:00.885
just to get the ketchup stains
off the desk.

00:17:00.885 --> 00:17:02.755
Then, it came time
for the closing statements,

00:17:02.755 --> 00:17:05.023
a chance for candidates to
direct voters to their websites

00:17:05.023 --> 00:17:07.392
or give them a number to text
to join the campaign,

00:17:07.392 --> 00:17:10.095
but when Biden had his chance,
he seemed to garble it.

00:17:10.095 --> 00:17:16.635
-If you agree with me,
go to Joe 30330.

00:17:16.635 --> 00:17:18.537
[ Laughter ]

00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:20.572
-Joe 3033--

00:17:20.572 --> 00:17:23.141
Is that the name of your
homemade rocket ship?

00:17:23.141 --> 00:17:25.076
[ Laughter ]

00:17:25.076 --> 00:17:28.614
Did you just accidentally tell
everyone your ATM PIN number?

00:17:28.614 --> 00:17:30.349
[ Laughter ]

00:17:30.349 --> 00:17:32.117
Is this some sort of weird clue?

00:17:32.117 --> 00:17:33.585
It's like being
in an escape room.

00:17:33.585 --> 00:17:35.153
"What does it say
under that lamp?

00:17:35.153 --> 00:17:39.524
Go to Joe 3033--
We need a clue master.

00:17:39.524 --> 00:17:42.728
Clue master!"
[ Laughter ]

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:44.396
It really doesn't work
when Joe Biden

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:46.231
tries to seem young and hip.

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:49.067
"Go to Joe 30330
on the world wide web.

00:17:49.067 --> 00:17:50.268
Hey, you know what?

00:17:50.268 --> 00:17:52.037
Throw a dot-com on there
if you want.

00:17:52.037 --> 00:17:53.438
[ Laughter ]

00:17:53.438 --> 00:17:54.672
Once again, the debate showcased

00:17:54.672 --> 00:17:56.275
sharp differences
on important issues.

00:17:56.275 --> 00:17:58.177
Whatever you think
of the candidates,

00:17:58.177 --> 00:18:00.344
it was nice to hear 10 people
speak coherently

00:18:00.344 --> 00:18:01.580
about actual policies.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:02.947
Meanwhile, Trump is probably

00:18:02.947 --> 00:18:04.582
wandering around
the White House,

00:18:04.582 --> 00:18:06.918
rambling to his aides about
how he's gonna be President

00:18:06.918 --> 00:18:11.156
until the year...
-30330.

00:18:11.156 --> 00:18:12.457
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:18:12.457 --> 00:18:16.662
[ Cheers and applause ]

